Seeds: [0, 1, 2] (each = fresh LO meta-training + 3 optimizee inits). Numbers are mean ± std over seeds; **test accuracy is measured once, after training**, at the final of 1000 optimizee steps. Hyper-parameters were chosen on a held-out validation split, never on test.

## Experiment: L1 regularizer

| Method | hyper-params | Test acc (%) | Test NLL | Val acc (%) | Train acc (%) | ‖θ‖₁ | frac(|θ|<1e-3) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1. MLP + AdamW | lr=0.01, wd=0.01 | **93.13 ± 0.08** | 0.2337 ± 0.0053 | 92.65 ± 0.21 | 96.56 ± 0.04 | 3324 | 0.005 |
| 2. MLP + AdamW + L1 | lr=0.01, λ=0.0001 | **93.75 ± 0.31** | 0.2090 ± 0.0069 | 93.40 ± 0.33 | 95.74 ± 0.28 | 1044 | 0.079 |
| 3. MLP + LO | meta-lr=1e-3 | **93.27 ± 0.16** | 0.2516 ± 0.0074 | 92.94 ± 0.20 | 95.89 ± 0.25 | 2407 | 0.008 |
| 4. MLP + LO + L1 | λ=0.001, + smoothing | **93.65 ± 0.48** | 0.2174 ± 0.0190 | 93.20 ± 0.24 | 95.85 ± 0.45 | 1251 | 0.013 |

Paired test-accuracy differences (same optimizee init + batch order):

- (2) AdamW+L1 − (1) AdamW : +0.62 ± 0.25 pp (3/3 seeds better)
- (4) LO+L1 − (3) LO       : +0.38 ± 0.52 pp (2/3 seeds better)
- (3) LO − (1) AdamW                  : +0.14 ± 0.13 pp (3/3 seeds better)
- (4) LO+L1 − (2) AdamW+L1 : -0.10 ± 0.63 pp (2/3 seeds better)
- (4) LO+L1 − diagnostic LO+smoothing-only : +0.23 ± 0.70 pp (2/3 seeds better)

## Experiment: L2 regularizer

